      "writtenOn": "2026-03-14T04:33:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The other day I said to claude \"the tests are failing\". It interpreted this as meaning \"I need to check the trybots\". However, we generally follow a different convention: we always explicitly refer to the trybots, otherwise a reference is to the local setup. i.e. \"the tests are failing\" is a way of me saying \"the tests in this project are failing when run locally\". If I had wanted to say \"the tests are failing our trybots\" I would have added \"trybot\" somewhere in the sentence to make clear.",
